  "id": "loafingaround",
  "neon": "#ffb34d",
  "note": "LOAFING AROUND — the bakery at the bottom of a terrace on Meltwater Row.\n\nThe tile's prose: the only window on the row that steams up from the inside; trays in the display\nat four in the morning and the good ones gone by seven; a sign shaped like a loaf with a slice cut\nout of it and the words running through the gap; the door paint worn to bare wood at hand height.\n\nSo the ground floor is a wide steamed window, lit warm, and the door beside it. The sign is a\ncrust-brown panel hung proud of the fascia with the name across it. Above it the terrace carries on\nfor two more floors of plain sash windows under a cornice, with a chimney stack for the oven.",
  "pal": "ty_oc_brick",
